course: dictionary
lesson: 3927
title: Reading a frown
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A frown is a look on the face. Your eyebrows come together and your forehead wrinkles. People frown when they are cross, worried, puzzled or thinking hard. «Suddenly the Queen stands in front of them, frowning like a thunderstorm» tells you she is very angry before she even speaks.
explain: You can read a frown the way you read a tricky word, by looking at the clues around it. Is the character shouting, or staring at a page of sums? A frown with tight lips often means anger. A frown while someone is thinking hard means they are puzzled.
explain: Frown can be a verb (to frown) or a noun (a frown). It also has a special meaning with «on». To frown on something means you disapprove of it, so «grannies frown on dropping bread» means they do not like it.
fact: A frown is when you bring your eyebrows together and wrinkle your forehead.
fact: You might frown when you are cross, worried, puzzled or thinking hard.
fact: To frown on something means to disapprove of it.
fact: A frown is the opposite of a smile.
fact: A quiet voice with eyes looking down may show that someone is sad or worried, not only frowning.
exercise: «Suddenly the Queen stands in front of them, frowning like a thunderstorm.» How does the Queen feel? | Sleepy | Happy and playful | *Angry | Hungry
exercise: A character frowns and stares at a page of sums for a long time. What is the most likely feeling? | Very hungry | *Puzzled or thinking hard | Bored and sleepy | Delighted
exercise: Grannies «frown on» dropping bread. What does frown on mean here? | Forget | Cover with flour | Hug | *Disapprove of
test: In the sentence «She gave him a deep frown», what kind of word is frown? | *Noun | Adverb | Verb | Adjective
test: «Turn that frown upside down» is a phrase. What does it ask someone to do? | Stand on their head | Walk away quietly | *Change a cross or sad look into a happy one | Put on a warm hat
exam: A character frowns, their eyebrows come together, and they stare at a tricky sum. What is the character feeling, and which clue tells you? | Sleepy, because their eyes are closed | Angry, because they are shouting | *Puzzled or thinking hard, because the eyebrows come together over the sum | Happy, because they are smiling
